* l2basic09 P8 steps 3 and 4: l2b09run has no compiler; it forks
* l2b09cc at start-up and LOAD goes through it.  The procedures run,
* list and replace older ones; KILL is passed on, so the compiler's
* copies go too (startrek fits after kill*); l2b09cc exits with us.
-x
chd /dd/l2b09
echo >term.out
/dd/l2b09/l2b09run #32k -t=/dd/l2b09/term.out <c.cmds >c.out >>c.err
procs >procs.out
* slot 7: l2b09run's code fits there now, so a 40K workspace starts
echo >term40.out
/dd/l2b09/l2b09run #40k -t=/dd/l2b09/term40.out <w.cmds >w.out >>w.err
